Fix: respect the configured menu_parent for top-level terms.

The condition negated getMenuParent(), so the configured parent menu item
(e.g. "Galerie") was only used when NO parent was configured — meaning never
when one actually existed. Top-level term links lost their parent and the menu
was flattened. Removing the "!" restores the hierarchy.

--- a/src/Entity/TaxonomyMenu.php
+++ b/src/Entity/TaxonomyMenu.php
@@ -270,7 +270,7 @@ class TaxonomyMenu extends ConfigEntityBase implements TaxonomyMenuInterface {

     // Note:
     // if menu_parent_id is NULL, it will not update the hierarchy properly.
-    if (empty($menu_parent_id) && !$this->getMenuParent()) {
+    if (empty($menu_parent_id) && $this->getMenuParent()) {
       $menu_parent_id = str_replace($this->getMenu() . ':', '', $this->getMenuParent());
     }

